## Feature #7 Increment 3 (spec §4.7) — Codex BLOCKER guard: deregistering a
## FIRED virtual timer must NOT (a) double-decrement `registered_count` (which
## would strand a still-pending timer) nor (b) touch the OS (a Linux
## `close((int)ident)` on a synthetic virtual handle would close an arbitrary
## fd — e.g. ident 1 = stdout). `ruxen_reactor_deregister` now has a virtual
## branch: clear the slot with no OS ops, decrement only if NOT already fired.
##
## This pin drives the reactor primitives DIRECTLY (the same calls
## `TimeSleepFuture` makes) so it deterministically reaches the deregister path
## — a `TimeSleepFuture` LOCAL would not auto-drop (the method-result drop-rooting
## limit), so we exercise deregister explicitly:
##   1. install virtual clock; register timer A (10s) + timer B (20s) → 2 live.
##   2. advance(10s) → A fires (check_fired(A)=1), B not yet.
##   3. DEREGISTER A (a FIRED virtual timer — the blocker path). Must be a no-op
##      on the OS + must NOT double-decrement (A was already decremented on fire).
##   4. advance(15s) (now=25s) → B fires (check_fired(B)=1). B firing proves its
##      wake/count path was NOT stranded by A's deregister. No crash / no closed
##      stdout proves the OS was untouched.

use std.time.Duration

def main
  puts "dereg start"
  TestClock.install
  var cx = Context.executor
  let h = ruxen_reactor_current_handle()

  let a = ruxen_reactor_register_timer(h, 10000000000)  # 10s virtual
  let b = ruxen_reactor_register_timer(h, 20000000000)  # 20s virtual

  TestClock.advance(Duration.from_secs(10))
  puts "a_fired=#{ruxen_reactor_check_fired(h, a)}"

  # Deregister the FIRED virtual timer A — the guarded blocker path. A was
  # already decremented when it fired, so deregister must NOT decrement again:
  # registered_count must stay at 1 (B still live), NOT drop to 0. (Without the
  # fix it double-decrements to 0, stranding park_current's fast-path.)
  ruxen_reactor_deregister(h, a)
  puts "count_after_dereg=#{ruxen_reactor_registered_count()}"

  # B must still fire (not stranded by A's deregister).
  TestClock.advance(Duration.from_secs(15))
  puts "b_fired=#{ruxen_reactor_check_fired(h, b)}"

  TestClock.uninstall
  puts "dereg done"
end
